   "source": [
    "# Uncertainty Estimation: Quantile Regression for Materials Confidence\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Abstract\n",
    "In materials discovery, point predictions are insufficient. We must estimate the confidence of our models, especially in unexplored chemical regions. This notebook explores **Quantile Regression** using CatBoost to provide 90% prediction intervals for perovskite band gaps, mapping the 'Epistemic Uncertainty' of the model to physical structural instability.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. The Model: CatBoost Quantile Regressor\n",
    "Quantile regression estimates the conditional quantiles of the target variable. Unlike standard regression which minimizes the Mean Squared Error (MSE), quantile regression minimizes the **Pinball Loss** ($L_{\\tau}$):\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "L_{\\tau}(y, \\\hat{y}) = \\\max[\\tau(y - \\\hat{y}), (1 - \\tau)(\\\hat{y} - y)]\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where $\\tau \\\in (0, 1)$ is the target quantile. By training two models at $\\tau = 0.05$ and $\\tau = 0.95$, we define the **90% Prediction Interval**:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "I(x) = [Q_{0.05}(x), Q_{0.95}(x)]\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. How the Model Interacts with Physics Data\n",
    "The model identifies 'Confidence Gaps' in the physical space where experimental data is sparse or the physics-to-structure relationship is inherently chaotic.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1. Aleatoric vs. Epistemic Uncertainty\n",
    "*   **Aleatoric (Data Noise):** Arises from experimental variance in lab measurements (e.g., different UV-Vis setups). The model captures this as a baseline interval width even in well-explored regions like $MAPbI_3$.\n",
    "*   **Epistemic (Model Knowledge):** Arises from a lack of training data. In regions where the **Tolerance Factor ($t$)** is far from 1.0 (highly strained lattices), the model predicts a wider interval, signaling that the 'Physical Ground Truth' is harder to pin down due to potential phase segregation.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.2. Mapping Physics Sensitivity\n",
    "For mixed-halogen perovskites ($MAPb(I_{1-x}Br_x)_3$), the band gap follows a non-linear 'Bowing' relationship:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "E_g(x) = (1-x)E_g(I) + xE_g(Br) - b \\\cdot x(1-x)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Where $b$ is the bowing parameter. The model's uncertainty increases in the mid-range ($x \\\approx 0.5$) because this is where the lattice is most sensitive to small stoichiometric fluctuations, leading to higher prediction variance."
   ],
